{"type":"plan","title":"Bánh Chưng Tết: Lễ Hội Của Bé An","logline":"Chiều Ba Mươi Tết, bé An học gói bánh chưng cùng bà, qua đêm canh nồi nghe chuyện xưa, sáng mùng Một thức dậy thấy chiếc bánh đầu tiên trên bàn thờ.","shots":[{"index":1,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Wide establishing shot of the tube house courtyard in golden afternoon light. Grandma sits on a low stool spreading dong leaves on a tray; little An stands beside her, bare feet on tiles, the charcoal stove and big iron pot behind them. Brick walls frame the open sky.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Chiều Ba Mươi Tết, bé An cùng bà gói bánh chưng trong sân nhà ở phố cổ Hà Nội.","cites":[]},{"index":2,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Medium shot from the side, afternoon light slanting across the tray. Grandma's wrinkled hands layer white glutinous rice, green mung bean paste, and seasoned pork onto glossy dong leaves; leaf veins catch the light. An watches from knee height.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Bà trải lá dong xanh lên mâm, đong gạo nếp trắng, nhân đậu xanh và thịt.","cites":[]},{"index":3,"shotType":"Low angle","description":"Low angle over Grandma's shoulder, afternoon glow. An's small hands mimic Grandma: folding leaf corners into a sharp square, then pulling pale bamboo strings tight in a grid. The first wrapped parcel takes shape on the tray.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"An học bà gấp lá thật vuông và buộc lạt tre thật chặt.","cites":[]},{"index":4,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Close-up on the finished square parcel in An's cupped hands, leaf texture and bamboo grid crisp in afternoon sun. Grandma's finger taps the corner; her eyes crinkle with pride. An beams, chest puffed.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Chiếc bánh đầu tiên An tự gói, bà khen vuông vắn như bánh của người lớn.","cites":[]},{"index":5,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Wide shot of the courtyard at night, lantern glow and charcoal fire painting the tiles orange. The big iron pot boils vigorously, steam rising. Grandma and An sit on stools on either side, silhouettes cosy against the flame.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Đêm xuống, nồi bánh sôi lục bục trên bếp lửa hồng giữa sân.","cites":[]},{"index":6,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Medium two-shot, firelight dancing on their faces. Grandma leans forward, voice low, telling the legend of Lang Liêu offering square and round cakes to King Hùng. An's eyes grow round, head tilted toward her.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Hai bà cháu ngồi canh nồi bánh, bà kể chuyện Lang Liêu dâng bánh cho vua Hùng.","cites":[]},{"index":7,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Close-up on Grandma's finger pointing at a square wrapped parcel resting on the stool's edge — square like the earth. An's face fills the other half of frame, eyes wide, breath held. Firelight flickers on the leaf veins.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Bà chỉ chiếc bánh vuông như mặt đất, An tròn mắt lắng nghe.","cites":[]},{"index":8,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Wide establishing shot of Hanoi old quarter rooftops at midnight. Terracotta tiles stretch into darkness, narrow alleys below. Fireworks burst overhead — red, gold, green — painting the tiles and two small figures on a rooftop terrace.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Đêm giao thừa, pháo hoa nở rực trên những mái ngói phố cổ.","cites":[]},{"index":9,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Close-up, fireworks reflected in An's drowsy eyes. Head rests on Grandma's lap, one tiny fist still curled around a pale bamboo string from the wrapping. Grandma's hand strokes the child's hair, silver bun glowing in the bursts.","mode":"still","dialogue":"An ngủ gục trên vai bà, tay vẫn nắm sợi lạt tre.","cites":[]},{"index":10,"shotType":"Pan","description":"Pan following An's bare feet pattering across the tiled hallway at dawn, pale blue light seeping through courtyard doors. The child dong. Grandma's silhouette fades behind as An darts toward the front room entrance.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Sáng mùng Một, An mở mắt và chạy ra phòng khách.","cites":[]},{"index":11,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Close-up insert on the small wooden table centred in the front room, dawn light pooling on its surface. The square wrapped parcel sits alone — glossy green leaves, visible veins, bamboo grid, dark corner folds. No altar drawn. The first cake An wrapped, offered to ancestors.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Trên bàn thờ là chiếc bánh chưng vuông vức đầu tiên do chính tay An gói.","cites":[]}]}
